    "result_text": "I changed keel back to **scaled + momentum + norm + thrust**, and `bin/e2e` passes.\n\n- **Server:** the keel formula in `src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/people/PersonView.java` now adds momentum once instead of twice, and its doc comment says so. Keel is still n/a when momentum or norm is.\n- **Front end:** I updated the comment on the `keel` field in `people.service.ts` to match. The page only shows the value the server sends, so no other front-end change was needed.\n- **Values that depend on keel:** fathom, draft, trim, ripple, ballast, the keel total and count, the \"countable\" filter and the rest are all built from keel, so they follow the new formula without further changes.\n\nI checked the expected numbers by hand as well. For Ada, scaled 36 + momentum 18 + norm 13 + thrust 15 = 82, which is what the test expects.\n\nThe front-end comments for beam and freeboard (\"keel times two\", \"keel divided by two\") don't match the server, which uses three for both. I left this alone because it's outside this change.",
